WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.030 --> 00:00:03.800
So, one frequent question that we get is

00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:06.700
now that you've found your WHY,
what do you do with it?

00:00:06.700 --> 00:00:07.600
How do you use it?

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:10.500
Well, one of the things you want to do is
keep it all around you.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:14.500
One of the things that I've done is
I actually would write my WHY on my desk,

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:15.131
next to my bed

00:00:15.131 --> 00:00:17.000
so that I was reminded of it.

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.100
That's number one.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:19.930
But also start talking about it.

00:00:19.930 --> 00:00:21.360
I start meetings with it.

00:00:21.360 --> 00:00:23.090
When I sit down with a meeting I say,

00:00:23.090 --> 00:00:24.400
before we start this meeting

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.900
I'd like to tell you why I took this meeting
or why I called this meeting

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:28.859
and I refer to my WHY

00:00:28.859 --> 00:00:30.800
and say how I believe 
that this potential partnership

00:00:30.800 --> 00:00:32.300
or this potential relationship

00:00:32.300 --> 00:00:33.977
could help me advance my cause,

00:00:33.977 --> 00:00:35.640
could help me advance my WHY.

00:00:35.640 --> 00:00:36.789
It works every time.

00:00:36.789 --> 00:00:40.350
It's extremely valuable in
resumes and interviews as well.

00:00:40.350 --> 00:00:40.966
When somebody says,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:41.800
so why do you want this job?

00:00:41.800 --> 00:00:42.300
You say,

00:00:42.300 --> 00:00:43.800
let me tell you why I do everything

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:46.000
and maybe tell a story from
your childhood or

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:49.350
one of the stories 
that you told in the WHY discovery process

00:00:49.350 --> 00:00:50.910
to communicate your point.

00:00:50.910 --> 00:00:53.250
I used to do that in all my interviews.

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:55.100
I still do it now.

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:56.129
I start meetings, I start talks,

00:00:56.129 --> 00:00:58.100
I start all kinds of things with it

00:00:58.100 --> 00:00:59.349
and it gives people a context for

00:00:59.349 --> 00:01:00.900
who you are
and where you're coming from.

00:01:00.900 --> 00:01:03.840
It's a huge advantage 
on resumes as well.

00:01:03.840 --> 00:01:06.727
I've never really understood 
at the top of resumes

00:01:06.727 --> 00:01:08.300
when people write "purpose"

00:01:08.300 --> 00:01:08.800
and they say

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.189
"to get a job at a top performing 
law firm blah blah blah ..."

00:01:11.189 --> 00:01:14.300
Of course, 
that's why everybody's applying for the job.

00:01:14.300 --> 00:01:17.493
Rather, use that space
at the top of your resume

00:01:17.493 --> 00:01:18.564
to explain who you are,

00:01:18.564 --> 00:01:20.900
basically WHY you do what you do.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:25.229
It gives context to all the other
jobs you've ever had.

00:01:25.229 --> 00:01:26.875
It gives context for who you are

00:01:26.875 --> 00:01:29.549
and it helps us 
stand out in the crowd of people

00:01:29.549 --> 00:01:31.573
who have similar experiences to us.

00:01:31.573 --> 00:01:34.380
It also helps us understand sometimes

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:35.615
where relationships fail.

00:01:35.615 --> 00:01:38.549
Where we sometimes did things
or said yes the things that

00:01:38.549 --> 00:01:39.795
in our guts it felt wrong

00:01:39.795 --> 00:01:41.220
but if we compare to our WHY

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:43.700
we realize that
we should never have done it in the first place.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:44.800
So use it
front and center.

00:01:44.800 --> 00:01:45.437
Speak about it.

00:01:45.437 --> 00:01:46.560
Tell the stories.

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:50.000
Use the stories as metaphors to
explain who you are.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.000
Talk about it constantly.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:52.000
Start meetings with it.

